WEBVTT

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.080
Yuki!

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.120
--Yuki?
--Oh, sorry.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.160
Can I call you "Yuki"?

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.870
I guess. What is it?

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.620
Let's walk home together!

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.290
--Ow!
--What if people find out
we live in the same dorm?

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.870
--What if people find out
we live in the same dorm?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.830
Huh?

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:42.870
Listen, Wonder Boy. People are bound to
tease us if they find out we do theater.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:48.040
Oh, you're right. People will
make fun of us if we're seen together.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.790
Call us "double shorties" or "the runt duo."

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.950
You insulted me without meaning to.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.120
S-Sorry.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.750
Anyway, just don't make it too obvious.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.290
O-Okay.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.410
'Sup, guys!

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.700
Those uniforms are totes adorbs!

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.290
Wait, why're you guys walking so far apart?

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.450
Camouflage.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:13.160
Ooh, what? It's like you're celebs! So cool!

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.910
It's a Porche!

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:24.950
Whoa, this your ride, Tenten? Sweet!

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.450
Stop being so loud in the middle of
the street. So embarrassing.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:32.410
You're more embarrassing, driving into
this narrow street with that flashy car.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.540
What's embarrassing about my car?!

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.750
Its <i>owner</i>.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.290
--C'mon, guys,
the yelling's attracting attention.
--Hey, you see them?

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.410
--C'mon, guys,
the yelling's attracting attention.
--Yeah, don't grow up to be like <i>that</i>.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:40.910
--Yeah, don't grow up to be like <i>that</i>.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.700
Igawa, you can head back.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.660
But...

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.870
I'll walk from here.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.410
Think that's his manager?

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.200
He's got a manager to
drive him around. That's our Tenten!

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.410
Get a move on! I'm leaving you behind!

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.700
There he goes again.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:38.000
"The Thousand and One Nights"
We'll now start Summer Troupe's first rehearsal.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.120
"The Thousand and One Nights"
But since we mostly have beginners here,
we'll start with some etudes.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:43.120
But since we mostly have beginners here,
we'll start with some etudes.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.290
What are etudes?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.080
You don't even know that?

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.120
Right, please explain, Tenma!

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.950
An etude is an improv exercise
where actors ad-lib as they act...

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.700
Wait, why the heck do I have to explain?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.000
You complain, but you still had
a fab explanation!

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.500
Go ahead and pair off.
Come up with your own setup.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.040
First, we'll have Yuki and Muku.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.200
--Right.
--Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.910
Ready, start!

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.000
What's up?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.540
H-Huh? Wh-What's up?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:26.120
Like, got anything fun to do?

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:30.120
School's been <i>so </i>boring recently.
I need something to do.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.620
High school girls.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.700
Yukki doesn't feel awkward at all.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:37.830
I-I'm, like, bored, too. Wanna hang out?

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.620
Like, totally. Wanna go for some karaoke?

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.040
Y-Yeah.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.790
Which one do you wanna go to?

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:49.120
Which one? Um... Oh, how about
the new one near the station?

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.080
Yeah, let's go there.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.290
Okay, stop there!

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.120
You both did a great job for your first time.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.290
They were both themselves
and just added "like" to everything.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.580
That's fine for their first time.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:04.700
Next up, Kazunari and Misumi.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:05.540
Roger.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.660
Triangle?

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.330
Ready, start!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.790
Hm... Oh, I know!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:21.120
Shoot, gotta get to my photo shoot.
Got a magazine interview after that, too.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.040
What are you doing?!

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:22.870
Huh?

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:26.450
Hurry, this way! I called
a taxi already, so get in!

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.410
Huh? Oh, a taxi?

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.910
I told you to be sure to review your schedule!

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:34.790
Y-Yeah, my bad.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:36.660
That weirdo's...

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.000
Really good.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.700
And make sure to pick up your phone!

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:43.620
S-Sorry, I didn't hear it.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:44.750
Okay, stop there!

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.660
You were both great!

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:52.500
Let's have Tenma and... Misumi, you go again.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.540
Okay.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.660
Start!

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:10.910
What?

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:14.330
What do you mean "what"? I can't look?

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:16.370
If you've got something to say, spit it out!

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.950
Stop trying to pick a fight!

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.910
You never change.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:23.790
Always wanting a fight,
even though you're my little bro.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.620
Acting like a big bro now, huh?

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.750
You rarely come home. Don't be so arrogant!

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.500
You know nothing about Dad's illness.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.500
Tenma's doing a good job adjusting
the story based on his partner.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.500
Illness? What are you talking about?!

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:41.450
It's none of your business.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:45.040
Of course it is! What are you talking about?!

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:54.910
Sorry. Tell me which hospital Dad's at.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.700
I'll drive.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:59.200
Thanks.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.290
Okay, that's good.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:05.370
You had all the elements
of a story. Excellent job.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.250
Now <i>that </i>was an etude.

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:11.120
Just saying stuff off the top of
your head like you guys won't work.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:15.660
Does he have to criticize every single thing?

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.250
I wonder why she asked us
to all meet after dinner.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.620
I'm gonna crash soon.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.500
Is everyone here?

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.540
Hey, it's Tsuzuroon!

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:29.370
'Sup.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:33.410
There are still many things
we need to figure out,

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:37.040
but first, we need to decide
who will be Summer Troupe's leader.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:37.910
Leader?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.450
It'll be me. Anyone else in this group
is out of the question.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:45.750
What?! Your big head is so inflated,
it's about float off.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:46.620
What the hell?!

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.450
Oh, maybe I'll give it a shot.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.080
--No way.
--Aw.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.700
I'm <i>not </i>having this flirt as my leader.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.830
I'm fine with anyone.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.620
--That's irresponsible!
--Hm...

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.200
What do you think, Muku?

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.870
Huh? U-Um...

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:07.450
I think Tenma, because he has
the most experience

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.580
and can instruct the rest of us on acting.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.790
You serious?! Acting's <i>all </i>he can do!

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.750
What do you mean it's <i>all </i>I can do, huh?!

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:14.790
That's enough!

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:18.870
Muku has a point,
so we'll have Tenma be the leader.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.160
What?!

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.290
Of course.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:25.790
However, Tenma, you must reflect on
how to act like a proper leader.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.500
You don't have to tell me. I was born a leader.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:32.200
That's exactly what she's telling you not to do.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.450
What'd you say?!

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:39.000
Settle down. Next, you'll decide the theme
of your debut performance with Tsuzuru.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.750
I don't care as long as there'll be triangles.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.950
Come on, you'll be in it, too,
so we need your input.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.000
Mm... Okay!

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.410
Kaz is very caring, huh?

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:53.290
That's Friendly McExtrovert for you.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:57.290
That's 'cause Sumi and I are buds, huh?

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:59.160
I'm buds with Kaz!

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:00.830
Yeah!

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:05.200
So how did Spring Troupe decide?

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.830
We followed in the footsteps of
original Spring Troupe's tastes.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:10.040
Should Summer Troupe do that, too?

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.660
I'm down.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:15.620
Wait, what was original Summer Troupe like?

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.580
They were a lively bunch
that specialized in comedy.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.700
Comedy?

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.620
What, have more to complain about?

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:25.040
No! Comedy just doesn't really suit me.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.120
You <i>are </i>complaining!

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.290
But Tenma might be right.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.120
What?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:34.000
It <i>is </i>harder to make people laugh than cry...

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.080
So maybe it's too big a challenge for you now...

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.160
I never said I wouldn't do it!

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.290
Comedy, huh?

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:44.450
It would be a good way to
expand my acting repertoire...

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:47.910
We'll follow in original Summer Troupe's
footsteps for our debut show!

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.120
She's got you wrapped around her finger.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.370
Is there anything else, Tsuzuru?

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:59.160
Yeah... I'm planning to
precast before writing again,

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:02.040
so if they could decide who will be
lead and secondary lead?

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:06.040
Lead role, huh? Anyone want to step up?

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:11.290
--Me, of course.
--I-I'd like to.
--Ooh, me, me, me!
--I wanna be lead.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.040
I can't believe they all want to.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:16.790
Give me a break! You want to
be lead at your levels?!

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.040
Gotta stand out, y'know?

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.660
I can make a gorgeous costume for myself.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.750
I can be a hero if I'm lead.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:24.250
Triangle's gotta be the lead.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.330
Hell no! We can't have an amateur do it!

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:29.750
Sakuya was lead without any experience.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.200
He was a special case.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:36.250
I'm glad they're motivated,
but they all want to be in the spotlight...

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:38.580
Complete opposite of Spring Troupe, huh?

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:41.330
Should we decide on the lead later?

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:48.160
No... Having all leads might just work out!

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:19.950
It's ready! Curry's what's for dinner tonight!

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.700
Invasion from Planet Curry.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:22.660
Curry <i>again</i>.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.160
We had curry yesterday and the day before!

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.700
Don't you think Director's curry is yummy?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:31.160
I'll pour curry on a triangular onigiri.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.750
Tsuzuroon, you okay?!

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.790
I-I finished!

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.660
Tsuzuroon!

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.540
--H-Hey!
--C-Call an ambulance!

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.330
Want an onigiri?

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:51.910
Huh?

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.790
H-He's asleep?

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:04.620
He pulled all-nighters writing again.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.000
Tsuzuroon, you okay?

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.700
Oh, sorry. I suddenly couldn't
keep my eyes open.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:18.500
You scared us.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.660
Seriously.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:22.040
Oh, how's the script?

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:28.830
Yeah, it's great! We'll go with this!

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:31.830
What's it about?

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:36.160
You all wanted to be lead,
so I based it on <i>Arabian Nights</i>.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:38.500
It's <i>The Thousand and One Nights</i>, right?

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.330
Yep.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.040
What's that about again?

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:45.410
It's about a princess who tells many stories.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.160
Yeah, lots of main characters show up.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.200
Do I play a triangle role?

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.870
Sorry, there isn't one.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.000
Aw.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.160
Tenma, troupe leader,
will play the main lead, Ali Baba.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:57.290
Of course.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.290
Yuki will be Scheherazade.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:02.750
It'll be fun to make the costume
for a princess from <i>Arabian Nights</i>!

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:04.500
Miyoshi will be Aladdin.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.160
Famous and showy!

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.000
Muku will play Sinbad.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:11.330
Sinbad's a hero, right? How wonderful!

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:13.660
And Ikaruga will be the genie of the lamp.

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.500
Kinda triangly. I like it!

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:20.580
You really solved the lead role problem.
Great job, Tsuzuru!

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:21.580
Yep!

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:24.580
You'll leave the costumes to me, then?

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.290
--Of course!
--Yes!

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:28.790
--You sure? If the costumes
look cheap, they'll be--

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:31.700
--Organdy and sequins!
--You sure? If the costumes
look cheap, they'll be--

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.660
I've got lots of great ideas!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:37.250
'Kay, I'll draw up some designs
to match the costumes.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.040
Can I let you handle that again?

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:44.500
Everything'll be handmade?
Is this really gonna work?

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:49.910
Yuki!

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:56.120
Oh, sorry. I need to walk far apart, right?

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.910
That you, Sakisaka?

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:00.370
Been a while.

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.200
Y-Yeah...

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.410
What've you been up to lately?

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.120
Nothing much, really.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.410
I see.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:12.580
C'mon.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.540
Gotta go. Gonna be late to practice.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.750
Okay. Good luck.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.580
Former teammates?

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:23.660
Huh?

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.660
From the track team.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.580
You knew?

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:30.080
Well, yeah.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:35.410
Everybody knew about
our star sprinter, Muku Sakisaka.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.660
You know about my injury, then, too?

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:40.120
Yeah.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:46.000
There's a hero from a <i>shojo </i>manga series
who was the track team star.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.580
They were so cool.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.750
You looked up to them,
so you joined the track team?

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.000
Yeah.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:59.620
I wanted to be a cool star like them
and practiced every day like crazy.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:02.700
I dreamed to win with this team.

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:04.790
But...

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.910
You had a good team?

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:08.410
The best.

00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:15.330
I can't chase after the dream
I shared with them anymore.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:22.290
So instead, I want to be like
a prince from <i>shojo </i>manga.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:26.790
They'd tease me if they found out, huh?

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.620
You're embarrassed about it?

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.950
Huh? Not really.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:36.160
You should invite them to our show.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.950
Have them watch our performance.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.370
But...

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.290
You found a new dream, didn't you?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.620
Yeah.

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:50.330
Then you should tell them.

00:15:55.870 --> 00:16:00.040
Yeah. Have to work hard at rehearsals, then!

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:04.450
Let's go. That hack will
complain again if we're late.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:06.750
You don't mind me walking with you?

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.500
Do whatever.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.080
Did you all read over the script thoroughly?

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.120
--Yeah.
--Of course.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.660
Let's start from the top.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:32.200
Tonight I have another tale to share with you.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:35.080
One of a thousand tales
that capture the imagination.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:39.410
Tell me, Scheherazade!
Where is the legendary paradise Oasis?!

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:43.540
Then, I will spin another tale for you tonight.
Long ago, in a faraway land--

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.750
Just cut to the chase!
Give it to me in four words or less!

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:49.290
--Aladdin. Magic lamp. Magician.
--Yuki's still feeling his way through,
but Tenma's already got his character down.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.830
--Yuki's still feeling his way through,
but Tenma's already got his character down.

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:55.660
Aladdin? Am I supposed to know
who that is? Ah, who cares.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:59.000
I gotta say, you're a real cutie-pie.
What's your name?

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:03.450
It'll be easy for Kazunari to be
a flirty Aladdin. It <i>was </i>written for him.

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:07.450
I shall grant you three wishes. Name them.

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:09.080
Yeowch! My butt's on fire!

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:12.200
--Can't you tell what I want?! Do something
about the magician and the serpent!

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:12.500
--The role's perfect for Misumi.
--Can't you tell what I want?! Do something
about the magician and the serpent!

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:14.000
--The role's perfect for Misumi.
--The magician and the serpent?
Dealing with both will use two of your wishes...

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:17.250
--His quirkiness lends to
the otherworldliness of the genie.
--The magician and the serpent?
Dealing with both will use two of your wishes...

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:18.450
That leaves...

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:22.660
Um... Grow up, Ali Baba.

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:25.580
There is no legendary paradise.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:28.500
You're not going to get rich--

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:31.580
Hey, you're not reading aloud
for class, you know.

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:33.250
S-Sorry!

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.700
Grow yup--up...

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:38.870
I'm sorry.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.910
Can you quit making him stop?

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.120
You're blaming me?!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:45.120
I'm sorry! It's because I'm a stupid,
dumb piece of tissue trash...

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.700
Nobody said that!

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:48.750
I-I'm sorry!

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:54.910
I'll get your damn water, geez!
Maybe I rushed into this too fast...

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:59.040
And that's the end. We got through
the whole thing for now.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:00.410
This is ridiculous.

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:03.790
You all think that level of acting
can match mine?

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:07.540
Especially you, Sakisaka!
You can't even read your lines!

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.370
Stop!

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:12.620
You can't expect them to be on
the same level as you from the start!

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:13.700
But...

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:18.790
As leader, think over how you can
help improve everyone's acting.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:24.040
What the hell. So it's <i>my </i>fault?

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:28.660
I have confidence in you, Tenma.

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.540
I've had enough.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:33.250
Keep practicing without me!

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:41.700
He's gone.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:45.000
It's fine. Just ignore his tantrum.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:49.330
Muku, cheer up.

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.750
You can have this triangle.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:52.950
Oh.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:02.830
Thank you.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.500
They can't act to save their lives!

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:11.290
And she wants me to figure out
how to help them? It's impossible!

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:15.120
Man, why's it seem like it's <i>my </i>fault here?

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.700
I didn't do anything wrong.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.910
Oh, Tenma?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:27.750
What's up? You're still
in the middle of rehearsal, right?

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.870
Finished for the day.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:33.370
I see. Good work.

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:34.500
Hey.

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:38.870
You're Spring Troupe's leader, right?

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:41.580
How was Spring Troupe?

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.620
What do you mean?

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:48.870
I mean, did you fight and have issues?

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:52.370
Ah, it was pretty tough at the beginning.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:57.620
We all got depressed when this guy,
Yuzo, picked us apart.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:59.330
Then what happened?

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:03.790
Mm, the director gave each of us special tasks.

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:05.950
You didn't do anything?

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:08.790
Me? Not really.

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:11.160
And it worked out just like that?

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.410
Yeah!

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:15.290
After we got to know each other better,
we were naturally able to communicate,

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.080
and our acting improved.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.410
Get to know each other?

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:22.660
It's more important for
each individual to do their best.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:29.080
Hm... It's hard to explain,

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.830
but I know because I actually experienced it.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:38.120
When your heart pounds because everyone's
emotions are engaged to the max.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:39.910
That feeling.

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:54.160
I hate to say it, but your acting on
closing night was remarkable.

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:56.370
Oh, and also...

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.950
"The Thousand and One Nights"

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:22.330
Summer Troupe's got a lot to overcome, too.

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:25.040
It's me.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.790
Tenma?

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.450
It's late. What is it?

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:34.120
As their leader, I figured out how to help them.

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:35.450
--Huh?
--I have a brilliant idea based on
my research. You wanna hear?

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:38.500
--I have a brilliant idea based on
my research. You wanna hear?

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:41.200
Yeah. Will you tell me?

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:45.830
For now, we'll all sleep together!

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:50.290
What?

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:53.410
What?

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:54.910
Th-That's it?

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:57.200
Yeah.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:00.370
It's based on my research.

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:05.540
Together...?

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:09.830
That might be a fantastic idea!

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:16.080
I thought of it, so 'course it is!
